# Generated / vendored content that root-level formatting must not touch.
#
# apps/server and apps/storefront are official scaffolds (Vendure /
# Next.js). Their own formatting conventions are managed by their own
# tooling (apps/storefront already ships its own eslint.config.mjs);
# forcing our root .prettierrc over generated framework code (including
# non-JS/TS assets like Vendure's MJML/Handlebars email templates, which
# Prettier's HTML parser cannot even parse) would be exactly the kind of
# unnecessary rewrite FOUND-015 explicitly avoids. See ADR-0013 and
# MASTER_IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md Phase 1B (FOUND-015 stop condition).
apps/

# The prior static-prototype repository, kept for reference only during
# FOUND-020 porting -- not something we maintain or reformat.
_reference/

# Generated lockfile -- never hand-formatted or Prettier-checked.
pnpm-lock.yaml

# The source of truth is an externally-governed authoritative document
# (SOT precedence rule, AGENTS.md / docs/internal note) -- we don't
# reformat its whitespace/line-wrapping as part of our own tooling.
docs/internal/

# The external build brief carries a generated 451-row SHA-256 manifest table
# and a generated directory tree, both injected by
# scripts/generate-manifest.mjs --inject. Prettier's table alignment would
# rewrite every generated row on each regeneration, so the document formats
# itself through the generator instead.
docs/implementation/ROCKET_NEW_BUILD_BRIEF.md
